[
  {
    "text": "The WorldLines paper proposes a specific translation technique as a component of its framework, but does not assert that the problem of translating long-term memory into embodied plans is completely solved or trivial.",
    "topic": "Solution Completeness"
  },
  {
    "text": "Classifying a task as a subproblem of partial observability and overwritten world states defines its scope but makes no claim about its difficulty or current state of the art.",
    "topic": "Problem Classification vs. Difficulty"
  },
  {
    "text": "The paper’s use of the translation as a motivated solution component does not preclude it from remaining an open research challenge; the paper may explicitly acknowledge limitations or need for future improvement.",
    "topic": "Acknowledgement of Limitations"
  },
  {
    "text": "Treating the translation as both a subproblem and a method is consistent: the framework identifies the need (motivation) and provides one possible solution mechanism, but other or better mechanisms could exist.",
    "topic": "Consistency of Dual Role"
  }
]
